## Interface: 11509, 16001
## AllowLoadGameType: vanilla, tbc, camelot
## Title: ZacUI |cff33ff99World map|r
## Notes: One seamless world map: every zone stitched together, zoom out of one into the next. Built on OpenMap (MIT, credited in LICENSE.txt). /openmap
## Author: Zac (map engine: OpenMap contributors)
## Version: 3.0.1
## IconTexture: Interface\AddOns\ZacUI\Media\addonIcon
## AddonCompartmentFunc: ZacuiWorldMap_OnAddonCompartmentClick
## AddonCompartmentFuncOnEnter: ZacuiWorldMap_OnAddonCompartmentEnter
## AddonCompartmentFuncOnLeave: ZacuiWorldMap_OnAddonCompartmentLeave
## SavedVariables: ZacuiWorldMapDB
## SavedVariablesPerCharacter: ZacuiWorldMapCharDB
## Dependencies: Zacui
## OptionalDeps: Questie, Leatrix_Maps, BetterMaps, HighFidelityWorldMap, HiddenMaps, Mapster, Magnify
## X-Category: Map
## X-License: MIT (code, from OpenMap v0.7.5-beta); map art is Blizzard's
## X-ZacUI-Part: WorldMap

# Part of ZacUI: the seamless world map. This is OpenMap (MIT,
# https://github.com/openmap-world/openmap) carried inside ZacUI so the
# one addon does it all, on Classic Era and WoW Forever alike. The
# engine keeps its own names (_G.OpenMap, ZacuiWorldMapDB, /openmap) so other
# addons that know OpenMap keep working and settings carry over. The
# licence is LICENSE.txt and the credits are Credits.lua - both stay.

Libs\Libs.xml

Core.lua

# Translations: only the client's own language's file loads (AllowLoadTextLocale: the other nine
# aren't read at all, a quarter of OpenMap's code by size; tools/locale/translate.py)
Locales\deDE.lua [AllowLoadTextLocale deDE]
Locales\esES.lua [AllowLoadTextLocale esES]
Locales\esMX.lua [AllowLoadTextLocale esMX]
